        "content": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\">\n<title>Help Seeking Among Undergraduate Men and Women in Engineering</title>\n<script>\nwindow.MathJax = { tex: { inlineMath: [['$', '$'], ['\\\\(', '\\\\)']], displayMath: [['$$', '$$'], ['\\\\[', '\\\\]']] } };\n</script>\n<script src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/mathjax@3/es5/tex-mml-chtml.js\"></script>\n<style>\n  * { box-sizing: border-box; }\n  body {\n    margin: 0;\n    background: #fff;\n    font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;\n    color: #111;\n  }\n  .poster {\n    width: 600px;\n    min-height: 427px;\n    margin: 0 auto;\n    background: white;\n  }\n  header {\n    height: 63px;\n    background: #080b20;\n    color: white;\n    text-align: center;\n    padding-top: 12px;\n  }\n  h1 {\n    font-size: 18px;\n    font-weight: 400;\n    letter-spacing: -.25px;\n    margin: 0 0 3px;\n    line-height: 1.05;\n  }\n  .authors {\n    font-size: 10px;\n    line-height: 1.05;\n  }\n  .affiliation {\n    font-size: 7px;\n    margin-top: 2px;\n  }\n  .content {\n    display: grid;\n    grid-template-columns: 32.5% 35.8% 31.7%;\n    padding: 7px 8px 5px;\n    column-gap: 7px;\n  }\n  .column { min-width: 0; }\n  .section-title {\n    color: #4a9b6d;\n    font-size: 10px;\n    font-weight: 400;\n    line-height: 1.05;\n    margin: 0 0 7px;\n  }\n  p {\n    font-size: 8px;\n    line-height: 1.13;\n    margin: 0 0 9px;\n  }\n  .emph { font-weight: 700; }\n  blockquote {\n    position: relative;\n    color: #777;\n    font-size: 11px;\n    font-style: italic;\n    line-height: 1.25;\n    margin: 6px 10px 10px 18px;\n    padding: 0;\n  }\n  blockquote:before {\n    content: \"“\";\n    position: absolute;\n    left: -15px;\n    top: -6px;\n    color: #b7d679;\n    font-size: 29px;\n    font-style: normal;\n    font-family: Georgia, serif;\n  }\n  blockquote:after {\n    content: \"”\";\n    position: absolute;\n    right: -4px;\n    bottom: -17px;\n    color: #b7d679;\n    font-size: 29px;\n    font-style: normal;\n    font-family: Georgia, serif;\n  }\n  .chart-title {\n    font-size: 5.7px;\n    line-height: 1.05;\n    font-weight: 700;\n    text-align: center;\n    margin: 2px 0 1px;\n  }\n  .chart {\n    position: relative;\n    height: 92px;\n    margin: 0 5px 0 2px;\n    border-left: 1px solid #999;\n    border-bottom: 1px solid #999;\n    background:\n      repeating-linear-gradient(to top, transparent 0, transparent 17px, #ddd 18px, transparent 19px);\n  }\n  .ylabels {\n    position: absolute;\n    left: -19px;\n    top: 2px;\n    height: 76px;\n    display: flex;\n    flex-direction: column;\n    justify-content: space-between;\n    font-size: 4.5px;\n  }\n  .bars {\n    position: absolute;\n    inset: 0 5px 0 16px;\n    display: flex;\n    align-items: flex-end;\n    justify-content: space-around;\n  }\n  .bargroup {\n    width: 33px;\n    height: 100%;\n    position: relative;\n    display: flex;\n    align-items: flex-end;\n    justify-content: center;\n  }\n  .bar {\n    width: 32px;\n    background: #29975e;\n  }\n  .bar.men { height: 25px; }\n  .bar.women { height: 54px; }\n  .xlab {\n    position: absolute;\n    bottom: -11px;\n    font-size: 5px;\n    color: #222;\n  }\n  .chart-foot {\n    font-size: 5px;\n    text-align: center;\n    margin-top: 10px;\n  }\n  .mini-chart {\n    height: 119px;\n    margin: 0 6px 4px 0;\n    position: relative;\n  }\n  .mini-chart .axis {\n    position: absolute;\n    left: 48px;\n    top: 10px;\n    width: 137px;\n    height: 93px;\n    border-top: 1px solid #d1d1d1;\n    border-bottom: 1px solid #d1d1d1;\n  }\n  .mini-chart .row {\n    position: absolute;\n    left: 0;\n    width: 100%;\n    height: 14px;\n    font-size: 4.3px;\n    color: #555;\n  }\n  .mini-chart .label {\n    display: inline-block;\n    width: 48px;\n    text-align: right;\n    padding-right: 4px;\n    vertical-align: middle;\n  }\n  .mini-chart .track {\n    display: inline-block;\n    width: 137px;\n    height: 10px;\n    vertical-align: middle;\n    background: #f1f1f1;\n  }\n  .mini-chart .fill { height: 100%; background: #777; }\n  .mini-chart .fill.light { background: #bbb; }\n  .r1 { top: 11px; } .r2 { top: 27px; } .r3 { top: 43px; }\n  .r4 { top: 65px; } .r5 { top: 81px; }\n  .caption {\n    font-size: 4.6px;\n    color: #555;\n    margin: -2px 0 7px;\n  }\n  .logo {\n    width: 51px;\n    height: 51px;\n    float: right;\n    margin: -5px 0 0 4px;\n    border-radius: 50%;\n    border: 2px solid #b58b35;\n    color: #123d67;\n    display: flex;\n    align-items: center;\n    justify-content: center;\n    text-align: center;\n    font-family: Georgia, serif;\n    font-size: 12px;\n    font-weight: bold;\n    background:\n      repeating-conic-gradient(#c99d40 0deg 4deg, transparent 4deg 18deg);\n  }\n  .logo span {\n    width: 31px;\n    height: 31px;\n    border-radius: 50%;\n    background: #174c75;\n    color: white;\n    display: flex;\n    align-items: center;\n    justify-content: center;\n  }\n  .tight { margin-bottom: 6px; }\n</style>\n</head>\n<body>\n<div class=\"poster\">\n  <header>\n    <h1>Help Seeking Among Undergraduate Men and Women in Engineering</h1>\n    <div class=\"authors\">J.W.<sup>1</sup>, J.F.<sup>1</sup>, E.P.<sup>2</sup>, and S.K.<sup>1</sup></div>\n    <div class=\"affiliation\"><sup>1</sup>Carnegie Mellon University, <sup>2</sup>Tennessee Tech University</div>\n  </header>\n\n  <main class=\"content\">\n    <section class=\"column\">\n      <h2 class=\"section-title\">Asking for help fosters student success</h2>\n      <p>Asking for help when necessary is critical to success in the workplace, but newcomers often fear how they will be perceived when they request assistance.</p>\n      <p>Understanding factors that motivate or inhibit various groups of students from seeking help can help us understand how to design interventions that will foster student success.</p>\n\n      <blockquote>Most of the time I’m very hesitant to go to their office. I feel like I’m always scared that they’re gonna think I’m an idiot when I walk in there.</blockquote>\n\n      <h2 class=\"section-title\">Women express concern about how they are perceived when seeking help</h2>\n      <p>We interviewed <span class=\"emph\">47 engineering undergraduates</span> about their help-seeking: <span class=\"emph\">32 women and 15 men.</span></p>\n\n      <div class=\"chart-title\">Respondents that Expressed Fear of Being<br>Perceived as Unintelligent or Underprepared</div>\n      <div class=\"chart\">\n        <div class=\"ylabels\"><span>50%</span><span>40%</span><span>30%</span><span>20%</span><span>10%</span><span>0%</span></div>\n        <div class=\"bars\">\n          <div class=\"bargroup\"><div class=\"bar men\"></div><span class=\"xlab\">Men</span></div>\n          <div class=\"bargroup\"><div class=\"bar women\"></div><span class=\"xlab\">Women</span></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"chart-foot\">Gender</div>\n    </section>\n\n    <section class=\"column\">\n      <h2 class=\"section-title\">Women report reaching out to more<br>resources than men</h2>\n\n      <div class=\"mini-chart\">\n        <div class=\"axis\"></div>\n        <div class=\"row r1\"><span class=\"label\">Tutor/Advisor</span><span class=\"track\"><span class=\"fill light\" style=\"width:39%\"></span></span></div>\n        <div class=\"row r2\"><span class=\"label\">Office Hours</span><span class=\"track\"><span class=\"fill\" style=\"width:36%\"></span></span></div>\n        <div class=\"row r3\"><span class=\"label\">Teaching Assistants</span><span class=\"track\"><span class=\"fill light\" style=\"width:58%\"></span></span></div>\n        <div class=\"row r4\"><span class=\"label\">Peers</span><span class=\"track\"><span class=\"fill light\" style=\"width:100%\"></span></span></div>\n        <div class=\"row r5\"><span class=\"label\">Professors</span><span class=\"track\"><span class=\"fill\" style=\"width:87%\"></span></span></div>\n      </div>\n\n      <p><span class=\"emph\">Over 90%</span> of women reported using two or more resources compared to less than half the men.</p>\n      <p><span class=\"emph\">Nearly 30%</span> (n=14) of the students we interviewed stated a strong preference to figure problems out themselves.</p>\n      <p>This sentiment was more commonly expressed by male students (40%) than female students (25%).</p>\n      <p>For some of our students, this independence manifested as a source of pride that <span class=\"emph\">prevented them from seeking help.</span></p>\n\n      <blockquote>I see most of the students are boys and they are very—I don’t know, maybe they get it better than I do. Sometimes I’ll feel maybe embarrassed to ask them questions</blockquote>\n    </section>\n\n    <section class=\"column\">\n      <h2 class=\"section-title\">Positive experiences encourage students<br>to ask for help</h2>\n      <p>Many students reported feeling more comfortable after a positive experience with an instructor who reached out to them and <span class=\"emph\">encouraged them, or expressed a clear passion for teaching.</span></p>\n      <p>Students reported developing strategies for asking questions. Most commonly doing as much of the work as possible in advance in order to form specific questions.</p>\n\n      <blockquote>I try to do all the work beforehand so I can point out to him exactly what’s going wrong, and why I’m not understanding</blockquote>\n\n      <h2 class=\"section-title\">Seeking help should be framed as an<br>academic competency</h2>\n      <p>Students need to be persuaded that knowing when to ask for help and how to ask competently are valued life-long skills.</p>\n      <div class=\"logo\"><span>NSF</span></div>\n      <p class=\"tight\">If students perceive asking for help effectively as an engineering competency, women and other marginalized students may experience fewer fears of stigmatization when asking questions.</p>\n    </section>\n  </main>\n</div>\n</body>\n</html>"
